    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#description": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "No Codes is a jazz collective formed by four musicians and composers: Benjamin Deschamps (alto saxophone), Frank Lozano (tenor saxophone), Sébastien Pellerin (double bass) and Louis-Vincent Hamel (drums). The group stands out for the absence of a harmonic instrument and for the emphasis placed on improvisation, interaction, and dialogue between the musicians.\n\nFollowing the success of their self-titled debut album released in 2018, the group is back in full force with Usual Suspects, launched in November 2024 under the Sunset Hill..."
      }
